8. Leads that came in before the automatic follow-ups existed and that nobody moved are in To do as a task "Follow up now" with their name: call or email them, then move the card.

### Owner referral links

An owner''s link for new owners is `carmacars.ca/r/<their code>?to=owner` (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner''s car. It shows under **Owner referral credits** as due; pay it with the owner''s payout and press **Mark paid**.

## Listing channels

Open **Marketing** > **Listing channels**: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).

1. Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press **Update** to change them, **Add a channel** for a new one.
2. None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel''s address: **JSON**, **CSV** or **XML** (the XML is in the shape of Google''s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.
3. Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner''s car (01 Motors or any other). **Keep out** takes a car out of every feed.
4. **New key** ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.

## Email campaigns

**Marketing** > **Channels** > **Email campaigns**. Everyone who gave us their email address on carmacars.ca gets the marketing emails: renters, customer accounts, leads from the site''s forms and addresses typed into forms that were never sent. Staff, owners as owners, Turo guests and leads typed in by staff are left out. Anyone who unsubscribes is never emailed again: the link is in every marketing email and takes effect at once.

1. **Audience** is how many addresses may be emailed now; **Waiting**, **Queued**, **Sent** and **Unsubscribed** follow.
2. **The weekly email** goes on the day and hour set below, with the cars listed now and the public promo codes running now.
3. **A new car**: when a car''s listing goes live (never a sample car), everyone gets one email about it, once.
4. Marketing emails go after every booking, payment and sign-in email, within the free daily email budgets (Cloudflare first, then Resend''s free plan). With **Send more marketing automatically** on, marketing uses what is left after the reserve; what does not fit waits for the next day. One campaign email a person a day at most.
5. **Switches and timing**: each campaign on or off, the day and hour of the weekly email, the reserve. Saving writes a new dated row of Program settings.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car&#39;s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week&#39;s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner&#39;s own profile, with a kit and a daily rotation under Marketplace.</p><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-facebook-marketplace" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Facebook Marketplace</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketplace</b>. Listings go up from the owner&#39;s own Facebook profile (business Pages cannot post vehicles), by Claude in the owner&#39;s Chrome or by a person. The playbook is docs/runbooks/marketplace.md.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> lists what is due: <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Take down</b> first, then up to the day&#39;s allowance of new posts and renewals (4 a day by default: 3 to 5 a day avoids spam flags). <b class="gd-ui">Coming up</b> shows the next days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Kit</b> on a car. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in the form&#39;s order (location, year, make, model, mileage, price, body style, colours, condition, fuel, transmission), each with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>, the description in Marketplace style, and the tracked link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the photos (ZIP)</b>. It has the 10 best photos named 01 to 10. Add them in that order: the first is the cover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post it. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> on Today and paste the listing&#39;s address. Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> the same way when you do those.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Inbox replies for this car</b> has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and &quot;send your number&quot;, filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car&#39;s link or asks for a phone number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">After answering the inbox, open <b class="gd-ui">Log an inbox session</b>. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today&#39;s. A price change marks the live listing <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b> and opens the usual update task.</li><li>A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says <b class="gd-ui">Do not post yet</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Rotation settings</b> change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car&#39;s home area wins).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The team&#39;s listings</b>: Sales post from their own profiles under <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b>, each listing in its own copy variant (title, description, photo order and cover), so no ad is posted twice. A car has at most 5 live listings, yours included (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Facebook Marketplace</b>). The card lists who posted what, its status, when it ends and the listing&#39;s address. Your own posts and renewals still count against your own day only.</li><li>The booking request asks &quot;How did you hear about us?&quot; (optional). Bookings by channel counts the answer after staff&#39;s source and a tracked visit.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-write-an-ad" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Write an ad</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Ads</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Ad listings</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press <b class="gd-ui">Write it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel&#39;s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post the ad on the site, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as posted</b> and paste its address and the date.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The text comes from the car&#39;s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.</li><li>The tracked link opens the car&#39;s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.</li><li>A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).</li><li>Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner&#39;s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-when-an-ad-needs-updating" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When an ad needs updating</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Posted ads</b>, or the task in <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff tasks</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A change of 3% or more in a car&#39;s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad&#39;s address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">New text</b>, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark the ad updated</b>. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Car off the site: take the ad down and press <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b>. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The 3% is under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-bookings-by-channel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings by channel</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings by channel</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter&#39;s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).</li><li>Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.</li><li>The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.</li><li>On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press <b class="gd-ui">Set</b> to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-facebook-page-and-instagram-drafts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Facebook Page and Instagram drafts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Social drafts</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The week&#39;s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price highlight or a seasonal trip (Facebook Page). Press <b class="gd-ui">Write drafts for this week</b> to write them now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read each draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> to change the caption, the channels or the day, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>; or press <b class="gd-ui">Skip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the caption for each channel (on the Facebook Page the tracked link is in the text; for Instagram copy the link for the bio), post it with the photos shown, then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted on Instagram</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Posted on Facebook Page</b> and paste the post&#39;s address.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Wednesday&#39;s walkaround video and Saturday&#39;s handover story are filmed by field staff. No renter is shown without written consent.</li><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a post of your own</b> at the bottom of the week for anything else.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-meta-publishing-off-until-set-up" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Meta publishing (off until set up)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Meta publishing</b>. Until it is on, every post is copied and posted by hand.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Make the Instagram account a professional account and link it to the CarmaCars Facebook Page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At developers.facebook.com, create a Business app owned by the CarmaCars business portfolio. Give it the permissions pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic and instagram_content_publish, and make a long-lived Page access token. Meta may ask for App Review before posts are public.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the details</b>: the Page id, the Instagram account id and the token. The token goes to the vault; the page shows only its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch on</b>. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove the token</b> at any time.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-scheduled-posts-facebook-instagram-tiktok" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Scheduled posts (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Social drafts</b>, the Scheduled posts card at the top. Sales have the same card on their Marketing page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose where (Facebook Page, Instagram or TikTok) and when. Pick a draft for its caption and link (and its photo), or write the caption. Pick a short video if you made one. Press <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every 5 minutes the database marks the posts whose time has come as due. With Meta publishing switched on, Facebook and Instagram posts go out by themselves (photos, Page videos and Instagram reels) and the post link is recorded; Meta refusing three times makes the post Failed with Meta&#39;s answer and a Try again button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Without Meta publishing the card says <b class="gd-ui">Connect Meta</b> and works as a queue: at its time a post is due with the caption to copy and the photo or video to download. Post it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted by hand</b> and paste the post&#39;s address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">TikTok is always by hand (its posting API needs TikTok&#39;s app review): a due TikTok post shows the checklist. Download the video, post it in the TikTok app with the caption, copy the link, press <b class="gd-ui">Posted by hand</b>.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Instagram needs a photo or an MP4 video; TikTok needs a video. Every change is in the post&#39;s Log.</li><li>Facebook Marketplace has no posting API: keep using the Marketplace kit and its session flow.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-short-video-for-reels-tiktok-and-stories" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Short video for Reels, TikTok and Stories</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing (below First photo) or in <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketplace</b>, the car&#39;s kit.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make a short video</b>. Your browser draws a 9:16 video from the car&#39;s approved photos: a slow zoom on each, the brand at the top, the car, the price a day and the call to action at the bottom. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved (about 20 seconds for 8 photos).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> to post it yourself, or schedule it in Scheduled posts. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes it off the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The words and timing are <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: social video call to action ({price} is the live price a day), brand, seconds a photo and photos a video. It is free: nothing is sent to a paid service.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-make-the-missing-angle" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make the missing angle</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing (below First photo) or in the Marketplace kit: for a required angle the car has no photo of.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make Rear</b> (or the angle missing). The image model makes that view from the car&#39;s approved photos, only within its free daily use (the showroom&#39;s limit).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the view: same car, same colour, wheels and badges, no damage hidden or added. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>An approved view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never used as damage or condition evidence (handovers, claims). Take the real photo when you can: a real photo of the angle replaces the view at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-recruitment" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner recruitment</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner recruitment</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a lead</b>: paste the ad&#39;s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call them with the script on the lead&#39;s page and press <b class="gd-ui">Log the call</b>. A yes needs their words (&quot;Yes, text me the details&quot;): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the lead&#39;s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. The email adds CarmaCars&#39; name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with &quot;Reply STOP to opt out.&quot; Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Record consent</b> for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no &quot;no solicitation&quot; note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).</li><li>The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.</li><li>A message without consent is refused with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner pipeline</b>. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of eight columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner&#39;s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner lead</b>. A visitor who starts the application is a lead as soon as a valid email or mobile is typed (Website form, unfinished), with the car they entered or priced in the earnings calculator; the same email or phone joins the lead already open.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press <b class="gd-ui">They replied</b>), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. <b class="gd-ui">Stop follow-ups</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Restart follow-ups</b> are on each card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Move</b> changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner&#39;s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service sees the same board in the staff portal. Sales see only the owners they invited, added or were given, on My sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new website lead goes to the least busy Sales person, never to a verification or test account (with no real Sales person on, it waits unassigned). Test accounts are never &quot;sourced by&quot; on a real lead or owner, nor given its task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">An application left unfinished for 30 minutes goes to the least busy Sales person with a task, and its follow-ups say &quot;finish your application&quot; with a link that opens their saved answers. When they send it, the card moves to Applied and the follow-ups stop.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Leads that came in before the automatic follow-ups existed and that nobody moved are in To do as a task &quot;Follow up now&quot; with their name: call or email them, then move the card.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Owner referral links</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s link for new owners is <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/r/&lt;their code&gt;?to=owner</span> (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner&#39;s car. It shows under <b class="gd-ui">Owner referral credits</b> as due; pay it with the owner&#39;s payout and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-listing-channels" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listing channels</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listing channels</b>: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to change them, <b class="gd-ui">Add a channel</b> for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel&#39;s address: <b class="gd-ui">JSON</b>, <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> or <b class="gd-ui">XML</b> (the XML is in the shape of Google&#39;s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner&#39;s car (01 Motors or any other). <b class="gd-ui">Keep out</b> takes a car out of every feed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-email-campaigns" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email campaigns</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Channels</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Email campaigns</b>. Everyone who gave us their email address on carmacars.ca gets the marketing emails: renters, customer accounts, leads from the site&#39;s forms and addresses typed into forms that were never sent. Staff, owners as owners, Turo guests and leads typed in by staff are left out. Anyone who unsubscribes is never emailed again: the link is in every marketing email and takes effect at once.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Audience</b> is how many addresses may be emailed now; <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Queued</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sent</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Unsubscribed</b> follow.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The weekly email</b> goes on the day and hour set below, with the cars listed now and the public promo codes running now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A new car</b>: when a car&#39;s listing goes live (never a sample car), everyone gets one email about it, once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Marketing emails go after every booking, payment and sign-in email, within the free daily email budgets (Cloudflare first, then Resend&#39;s free plan). With <b class="gd-ui">Send more marketing automatically</b> on, marketing uses what is left after the reserve; what does not fit waits for the next day. One campaign email a person a day at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Switches and timing</b>: each campaign on or off, the day and hour of the weekly email, the reserve. Saving writes a new dated row of Program settings.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'marketing-on-facebook-marketplace', 'chapter', 'sales', '**Sales** > **Marketing**. You post CarmaCars cars on Facebook Marketplace from your own Facebook profile, answer the Marketplace inbox, and log what you did. The numbers you collect are leads credited to you.

## Never the same ad twice

Each car can have up to 5 live listings across the team (the owner''s own listing included). Every listing is a different **copy variant**: its own title, its own description wording, its own photo order and its own cover photo. When you claim a car, its variant is yours until you take the listing down or it lapses: no one else can post that copy. You can have one listing of a car at a time.

- A claim you do not post within a day lets go by itself.
- A listing ends 30 days after you posted or renewed it, unless you renew it.
- The Admin sees who posted what, with the listing''s address.

## Today

1. **Today** lists your work in this order: **Take down**, **Update the price**, **Post it** (a car you claimed), then **Renew** and new **Post** items, up to your posts and renewals for the day (4 by default).
2. On a **Post** item press **Claim variant** with its number. Then press **Kit**.
3. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in order, each with **Copy**, your variant''s description and tracked link, and the photos in your order. Press **Download the photos (ZIP)**: 01 is your cover. **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the car''s marketing set instead (its photos in other scenes, made on its listing).
4. Post it on Facebook, open the new listing and copy its address. Back on **Today**, press **Posted** and paste the address. **Let go** frees a claim you will not post.
5. Press **Renewed**, **Updated** or **Taken down** when you do those on Facebook.

## Words to use

Nothing a buyer reads says "rent", "rental" or "for rent". Every listing keeps the line "Daily and weekly bookings only, not for sale" and the price is for one day. The kit and the replies already follow this.

## The auto-reply

**Auto-reply for this listing** has the steps and the text, with your listing''s own link. While posting, scroll to **Auto replies** (or **Meta AI replies**), turn it on, replace the draft with the text, then publish. It only answers the first "Is this available?".

## The inbox

1. Open facebook.com/marketplace/inbox, the Selling tab, oldest first.
2. Use **Inbox replies for this car** only: price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery, send your number. One message per reply, at most two to someone who does not answer.
3. Then **Log an inbox session**: the chats, the replies and every number, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number is a lead credited to you, with a call-back task within 15 minutes.

## Your own Claude

**Your Claude in Chrome** has the instructions to paste into Claude in your own Chrome, and the **Academy lesson** that teaches them. Claude follows the same rules: the kit''s words and the templates only, it stops at any Facebook security check or CAPTCHA and tells you, it never types a password, and it logs every post in your Marketing tab.

> Watch out: Stop and tell the Admin if Facebook removes a listing or restricts your account. Do not appeal and do not post it again.

## Event pages

Below Marketplace, **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Press **Add an event** for a new one, or **Edit** to set its dates once the organiser announces them, with the organiser''s page as the source. Share an event page in your posts in the weeks before it.', 'Marketing on Facebook Marketplace', 'Your own listings from your own profile, never the same ad twice, the auto-reply, the inbox and your Claude.',
